{
  "statement": "As the TrustworthinessAgent, I emphasize the critical nature of security and privacy in the RollCall system. TRU-01 ensures that all student attendance data is encrypted, safeguarding it from unauthorized access. TRU-02 establishes role-based access control, essential for protecting sensitive information. TRU-03 maintains an audit log for accountability in attendance records. TRU-04 ensures that students can only view their records post-authentication, enhancing data security. TRU-05 verifies data integrity through checksums, while TRU-06 allows users to report breaches, ensuring proactive security measures. TRU-07 enforces session timeouts, further enhancing user safety.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {"ids": ["SAF-06", "TRU-01"], "type": "logical", "description": "Manual overrides (SAF-06) may conflict with the encryption requirement (TRU-01) if not handled properly."},
    {"ids": ["TRU-02", "RES-06"], "type": "logical", "description": "Role-based access control (TRU-02) overlaps with the restriction of attendance data access (RES-06), requiring careful integration."},
    {"ids": ["TRU-06", "RES-05"], "type": "logical", "description": "Notifying students of attendance status (RES-05) must consider how unauthorized access is reported (TRU-06), ensuring secure communication."}
